NOTES: Build each cylinder as an open-ended CylinderGeometry with a transparent MeshPhysicalMaterial (transmission/opacity ~0.25) for glass, plus a slightly smaller opaque cylinder for the oil and a CircleGeometry meniscus. Spheres use MeshStandardMaterial with metalness~0.9, roughness~0.3 and an environment map for the metallic highlight. Drive sphere y-position in the render loop from per-grade terminal velocity; the slider recomputes the probe sphere's velocity continuously. Velocity labels are camera-facing Sprites shown/hidden by the toggle. Keep all four reference tubes static in color/grade; the slider controls a single highlighted probe sphere (e.g. brighten its tube) so the race animation and the continuous sweep do not conflict.

